\title{scroll: Interactive Single-Cell Explorers from Seurat Objects}
\description{
Turns a processed Seurat object into a polished, interactive single-cell explorer: a Shiny app of eight analysis panels (DimPlot, FeaturePlot, Biaxial, DotPlot, Violin, Proportions, and live differential expression including replicate-aware pseudobulk), each with its own controls. A heavy offline build phase extracts a compact, sparse on-disk store (cell metadata and embeddings as one Parquet table, expression as a one feature-sorted Parquet file per assay) that the app reads one feature at a time via 'arrow', so runtime memory stays flat regardless of matrix size. A streaming builder assembles multi-million-cell projects one source at a time.
